  "headline": "Government Opens 154,052 CPNS 2026 Positions Starting November 27",
  "seoTitle": "Pendaftaran CPNS 2026 Dibuka 27 November",
  "metaDescription": "Government opens 154,052 CPNS 2026 positions starting November 27, exclusively for central government and PHTC programs without local government formations.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Registration for 154,052 central government CPNS positions begins November 27, 2026, and will close in early December.",
    "Minister Rini Widyantini confirmed no regional government formations will be included in the 2026 recruitment process.",
    "Candidates may reuse their 2024 SKD test scores, and officials have guaranteed a transparent selection process free from corruption or influence."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government has announced the opening of the 2026 Civil Servant Candidate (CPNS) recruitment, offering 154,052 positions starting November 27, 2026. Minister of Administrative and Bureaucratic Reform (PANRB) Rini Widyantini confirmed that this cycle focuses exclusively on central government roles and the PHTC program, excluding regional government vacancies. To ensure transparency, authorities emphasized that test results will be provided immediately, and strict measures are in place to prevent corruption, collusion, or nepotism, including any improper influence from officials. Applicants are not required to use digital stamps for this cycle, and those who participated in the 2024 selection may opt to use their previous Basic Competency Selection (SKD) scores. The registration period is scheduled to last one week, concluding in early December 2026. Data from the National Civil Service Agency (BKN) indicates that 435,000 individuals have already registered accounts on the SSCASN portal.",
  "whyItIsViral": "The story is trending due to the significant volume of open positions and high-speed reporting across multiple news outlets regarding the specific registration timeline and policy changes for the 2026 recruitment cycle.",
